# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the host-side tests.
#
# The simulated DMA engine (tests/mock_hw.cpp) reads and writes the simulated peripheral registers and the
# DMA memory from its own thread while the code under test accesses them through volatile pointers, as it
# does with real hardware. Those accesses are not data races of the driver.
race:MockDmaEngine::Run
# The retune test polls the simulated PLL and GPIO registers from a monitor thread.
race:testRetuneCarrierOffAndReplay
# These tests write simulated registers directly to emulate the hardware (DMA halted, channel busy, a
# transmitter left running by a terminated process).
race:testDmaRestartAndPads
race:testDmaChannelSelection
race:testSessionLockAndRecovery
